# @defaultSensitive=false @defaultRequired=false
# ---
# Shepherd's environment-variable catalogue, checked by `bun run check:env-schema`
# (`varlock audit`) in CI and pre-push. Issue #2347; reasoning in
# docs/research/varlock-adoption.md.
#
# WHAT THIS FILE IS
#   A catalogue of Shepherd's environment surface, with each key's type and current default.
#   Two parts of it are COMPLETE, and one deliberately is not:
#     - complete: every variable Shepherd READS, except the ambient POSIX ones listed under
#       "NOT declared" below;
#     - complete: every SHEPHERD_*-namespaced variable Shepherd injects into a child — its own
#       contract, reconcilable with a single grep for the prefix;
#     - NOT exhaustive: third-party variables Shepherd pins onto child processes (Claude
#       Code's, git's, node's). The ones that explain visible agent behaviour are declared
#       below as a courtesy; there is no claim that the list is complete, because that surface
#       is injected through object-literal spreads and env(1) argv tokens that no grep
#       enumerates reliably, and it bleeds into shell variables inside generated scripts. It is documentation plus a drift gate — nothing loads it at runtime,
#   and Bun does not autoload `.env.schema`, so editing a value here changes no behaviour.
#   `src/config.ts` remains the source of the defaults.
#
# WHAT IT IS NOT
#   Not "Shepherd's configuration source of truth". Config is three stacked tiers —
#   process env, `src/config.ts` defaults, then the `settings` table — and the DB table
#   wins at runtime for most behavioural knobs. This file governs the env SEED layer.
#   No variable is required: a fresh install boots with none of them set, which is why
#   the header sets `@defaultRequired=false`.
#
# WHAT THE GATE CAN AND CANNOT SEE
#   `varlock audit` finds `process.env.KEY`, `process.env["KEY"]` and `import.meta.env.KEY`.
#   It is blind to shell scripts, to destructured `env.KEY`, to `process.env[SOME_CONST]`
#   and to keys passed as a string argument (`envNum("SHEPHERD_…", 30)`). Keys read only
#   that way are declared here with `@auditIgnore` so the "declared but unused" half of the
#   gate stays quiet — they are catalogued, not enforced. If you add a knob through one of
#   those patterns, the gate will NOT remind you to declare it.
#
#   There is also a scanner BUG worth knowing about, found while writing this file and
#   verified against varlock 1.19.0 with a minimal fixture: a regex literal containing a
#   quote character — /'/, /"/ or /`/ — makes the scanner lose every `process.env` reference
#   AFTER it in that file. A plain /abc/ is fine. The scanner is evidently not lexing regex
#   literals, so the quote reads as the start of a string. Ten files in src/ and scripts/ are
#   affected today (auth-mode.ts, codex-activity.ts, diff-annotations.ts, forge/checks.ts,
#   herdr-recovery.ts, herdr-update.ts, preview-launch.ts, visual-blocks.ts,
#   eval-fixtures/env.ts, check-model-mirror.mjs). Exactly ONE env read sits in a blinded
#   region — SHEPHERD_HERDR_RECOVERY_LOG, marked below — so coverage today is complete, but a
#   new knob added after such a regex would slip past the gate silently.
#
#   RECONCILING BY HAND. `process.env.KEY` is only half the story — a destructured
#   `const { env } = process` read (or any `env.KEY` parameter) needs its own sweep, and
#   missing it is how HERDR_SESSION and HERDR_ENV were left undeclared in an earlier draft of
#   this file. Both halves:
#     grep -rhoE 'process\.env\.[A-Za-z_][A-Za-z0-9_]*' src scripts deploy
#     grep -rhoE '\b(env|[a-zA-Z]+Env)\??\.[A-Z][A-Z0-9_]{2,}' src scripts deploy
#
#   INJECTION is a third shape again — `env.KEY = v`, an object literal `{ ...process.env,
#   KEY: v }`, an env(1) argv token `KEY=v`, or `--setenv=KEY=v`. Treat any grep for it as a
#   lead, not an inventory: a spread-with-literal such as
#   `{ ...process.env, GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT: "0" }` (src/repos.ts) evades all the obvious
#   patterns, which is exactly why the third-party half above is not claimed to be complete.
#   The SHEPHERD_* half IS complete, and stays checkable with:
#     grep -rhoE 'SHEPHERD_[A-Z0-9_]+' src scripts deploy | sort -u
#
# HOUSE RULES
#   - One line of description per key, in the same voice as
#     docs-site/src/content/docs/reference/configuration.md, which keeps the long prose.
#   - Every SHEPHERD_*-namespaced key without `@auditIgnore` MUST also have a row on that
#     page — enforced by `bun run check:env-schema-docs` (#2361) in CI and pre-push. A key
#     that is genuinely contributor-only rather than operator-settable carries `@docsExempt`
#     instead, and says in its description why. varlock ignores decorators it does not know,
#     so `@docsExempt` is invisible to `varlock audit`.
#   - The value is the CURRENT default. Where the default is derived (`SHEPHERD_DB` under
#     $HOME), computed (`SHEPHERD_AGENT_INGRESS_PORT` = port + 1) or too long to inline,
#     the value is left empty and the description states it. Never invent a literal.
#   - Kill switches (default ON) are written `=true`; opt-ins `=false`. Transcribe each one
#     from its read site — `src/config.ts` parses booleans five different ways and a
#     mechanical rewrite inverts every kill switch.
#   - Secrets carry `@sensitive` and never a value.

# ── Core: network, paths, roots ───────────────────────────────────────────────

# HTTP/WS listen port for the HUD. A non-integer or out-of-range value is rejected at
# boot, naming this key; unset falls back to the default.
# @type=port
SHEPHERD_PORT=7330

# Bind address. Loopback-only by default; `0.0.0.0` exposes every NIC (not recommended).
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_HOST=127.0.0.1

# Pinned loopback port for the auth-exempt agent-ingress listener (hook callbacks, the
# build-queue/epic-draft routes, the per-session MCP endpoint). Defaults to SHEPHERD_PORT + 1;
# `0` restores an ephemeral port. Validated at boot against the main, served and preview ports.
# @type=port
SHEPHERD_AGENT_INGRESS_PORT=

# SQLite session-store path. Default `~/.shepherd/shepherd.db`; the forges map, plugins dir
# and update logs all default to siblings of this file.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_DB=

# Path to the git-host config. Default: `forges.json` next to the DB.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_FORGES=

# Directory scanned at boot for server-side plugins. Default: `plugins/` next to the DB, so
# private extensions survive `bun run update` and never enter the public repo.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_PLUGINS_DIR=

# Repos must live under this root; agent spawn is confined to it. Defaults to $HOME.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_REPO_ROOT=

# Comma-separated origin hostnames allowed for writes and WebSocket upgrades (CSRF/CSWSH
# guard). The Capture extension IDs and every Tailscale-served host are appended at boot, so
# this is not the whole effective allowlist.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_ALLOWED_HOSTS=localhost,127.0.0.1,::1,[::1]

# Persistent audit log for `herdr update`, written by the transient update unit so the record
# survives the restart it triggers. Default: `herdr-update.log` next to the DB.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_HERDR_UPDATE_LOG=

# Same, for `codex update`. Default: `codex-update.log` next to the DB.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_CODEX_UPDATE_LOG=

# ── Operator authentication and secrets ──────────────────────────────────────

# Single-operator login password. When set it is authoritative — argon2id-hashed and
# re-seeded into the persisted hash every boot. Unset: the persisted hash is reused, or a
# strong password is generated and printed to the log once on first boot.
# @sensitive
SHEPHERD_PASSWORD=

# HMAC secret signing the session cookie. Set it to pin a stable secret across DB resets;
# rotating it invalidates every outstanding session.
# @sensitive
SHEPHERD_COOKIE_SECRET=

# Optional unscoped operator bearer for CLI/curl/machine clients, accepted instead of the
# session cookie. Break-glass credential — prefer a scoped token minted under Settings → Access.
# @sensitive
SHEPHERD_TOKEN=

# Authentication mode for spawned agents: `subscription` (OAuth) or `api-key`.
# @type=enum(subscription, api-key)
SHEPHERD_AUTH_MODE=subscription

# Path to a pre-existing apiKeyHelper script, used instead of the one Shepherd writes into
# the config dir under `api-key` auth mode. Unset: Shepherd manages the helper itself.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_API_KEY_HELPER_PATH=

# ── Web push (VAPID) ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# VAPID public key for Web Push. Unset: a keypair is generated and persisted on first use.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_VAPID_PUBLIC=

# VAPID private key. Pairs with SHEPHERD_VAPID_PUBLIC — set both or neither.
# @sensitive
SHEPHERD_VAPID_PRIVATE=

# VAPID JWT subject. Must be a valid `https:` or `mailto:` URL; Apple rejects anything else
# with BadJwtToken.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_VAPID_SUBJECT=https://github.com/erwins-enkel/shepherd

# ── Telemetry ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Seeds the persisted telemetry-consent state: `unset` (first-run prompt), `granted`, `denied`.
# @type=enum(unset, granted, denied)
SHEPHERD_TELEMETRY_CONSENT=unset

# Aptabase app key. NOT a secret — it is a client-side ingestion identifier, shipped in the
# public source. Forks set their own, or blank to disable telemetry entirely.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_APTABASE_APP_KEY=A-EU-2837516646

# Overrides the Aptabase ingestion host derived from the app key's region prefix.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_APTABASE_HOST=

# Cross-tool opt-out convention (consoledonottrack.com). `1` or `true` disables telemetry
# regardless of consent state.
# @type=boolean
DO_NOT_TRACK=false

# ── Agent runtime: herdr, Codex, node, Claude config ─────────────────────────

# Path to the herdr binary.
# @type=string
HERDR_BIN=herdr

# Unix-socket path for herdr's native JSON-RPC API. Unset: derived from HERDR_SESSION — a
# non-`default` session uses its own per-session socket, `default` uses herdr's top-level one.
# @type=string
HERDR_SOCKET_PATH=

# Opt-in: talk to herdr over its Unix-socket JSON-RPC API instead of shelling out to the CLI
# for every call. The driver falls back to the CLI on any protocol mismatch, so it is reversible.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_HERDR_SOCKET=false

# Interim sub-flag of SHEPHERD_HERDR_SOCKET: stream the browser terminal over herdr's socket
# instead of the node-pty helper. Default off — that stream is a screen-diff protocol, so
# xterm builds no scrollback and mouse/wheel scrolling stops working.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_HERDR_SOCKET_TERMINAL=false

# Path to the Codex CLI binary.
# @type=string
CODEX_BIN=codex

# Codex state directory (rollouts, usage). Default `~/.codex`.
# @type=string
CODEX_HOME=

# Explicit node binary for the PTY attach helper. Wins over resolution when non-empty —
# resolution exists because a mise/nvm-managed node is often absent from the launcher's PATH,
# and without it every session pane stays black.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_NODE_BIN=

# Base Claude Code config dir; the sandbox membrane's binds resolve from it. Default `~/.claude`.
# @type=string
CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR=

# Where Claude Code writes its session JSONL, used for usage tracking.
# Default: `$CLAUDE_CONFIG_DIR/projects`.
# @type=string
CLAUDE_PROJECTS_DIR=

# Claude Code's own scratch dir. Shepherd sets it at boot so scratch consumers follow trusted
# agents onto disk rather than tmpfs, and strips it from sandboxed spawns.
# @type=string
CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR=

# ── Sandbox and egress ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Default sandbox profile for spawned agents: `trusted` (unconfined), `standard` or
# `autonomous` (bwrap membrane plus, for autonomous, a netns egress firewall).
# @type=enum(trusted, standard, autonomous)
SHEPHERD_SANDBOX_DEFAULT_PROFILE=trusted

# Comma-separated extra hostnames always allowlisted by the autonomous profile's egress
# firewall, on top of the built-in Anthropic and forge hosts. No effect on trusted/standard.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_SANDBOX_EXTRA_HOSTS=

# Opt-in escape hatch for the fail-closed author-trust gate on autonomous drain: trust issue
# authors on forges that cannot supply a GitHub-style authorAssociation. Never relaxes the
# gate on GitHub.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_TRUST_ISSUE_AUTHORS=false

# Ingest Claude Code hook events instead of polling. Kill switch — default ON, `0` disables.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_HOOKS_INGEST=true

# Derive session signals from hook events. Kill switch — default ON, `0` disables; only takes
# effect on herdr <= 0.7.4.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_HOOKS_SIGNALS=true

# Pre-tool guard for spawned agents. Kill switch — default ON, `0` disables.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_TOOL_GUARD=true

# ── Session lifecycle ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Daily housekeeping sweep over already-archived sessions (retention window plus newest-N cap,
# cascading review rows). Kill switch — default ON; `0` seeds it off on a fresh DB.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_SESSION_HOUSEKEEPING=true

# Auto-archive finished sessions. Kill switch — default ON; `0` disables.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_SESSION_AUTO_ARCHIVE=true

# Seed the persisted auto-revive setting ON: restart agents whose pane died under them.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_AUTO_REVIVE=false

# Runaway-orphan reaper mode: `armed` (kill), `observe` (log only) or `off`.
# @type=enum(armed, observe, off)
SHEPHERD_REAP_RUNAWAY=armed

# Minimum sustained CPU fraction before the reaper considers a process runaway.
# @type=number
SHEPHERD_REAP_RUNAWAY_MIN_CPU=0.8

# Minimum process age in seconds before the reaper will touch it.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_REAP_RUNAWAY_MIN_AGE_S=300

# Trim the per-turn context of auto-spawned drain agents (optional plugins, bundled skills and
# your personal ~/.claude/skills disabled per spawn; the repo's own skills stay). Interactive
# sessions untouched. Default ON — `false`/`0`/`off` is the escape hatch.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_TRIM_AUTO_CONTEXT=true

# Overrides the built-in prompt used by the "standard" task kind. Unset: the bundled German
# "is this issue still relevant" prompt. A customized `standardCommand` setting wins over both.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_STANDARD_COMMAND=

# Character budget for the house-rules block injected into agent prompts.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_HOUSE_RULES_BUDGET_CHARS=4000

# ── Model, effort and provider defaults ──────────────────────────────────────

# Default agent provider for new sessions.
# @type=enum(claude, codex)
SHEPHERD_DEFAULT_AGENT_PROVIDER=claude

# Seeds the persisted default Claude model. `auto`, `default`, or any known Claude alias.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_DEFAULT_MODEL=auto

# Seeds the persisted default Codex model. Any curated Codex alias.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_DEFAULT_CODEX_MODEL=gpt-5.6-sol

# Seeds the persisted default reasoning effort.
# @type=enum(default, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra)
SHEPHERD_DEFAULT_EFFORT=default

# Seeds the "Fable available" setting. When off, an argv-only fable→opus fallback applies while
# the stored model stays `fable`, so pricing and replay stay correct.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_FABLE_AVAILABLE=true

# Operator language for agent-facing directives and generated prose.
# @type=enum(en, de)
SHEPHERD_OPERATOR_LANGUAGE=en

# ── Role agents ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Every role takes a CLI / model / effort triple. `inherit` means "whatever the session's own
# provider is"; `default` means "no explicit flag". Model tokens are validated against the
# union of both providers' aliases, so they are typed `string` rather than a brittle enum.

# PR critic — reviews a green PR and posts a verdict.
# @type=enum(inherit, claude, codex)
SHEPHERD_CRITIC_CLI=inherit
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_CRITIC_MODEL=default
# The critic is a rigor role; anything below `high` weakens PR review and is warned about at boot.
# @type=enum(default, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra)
SHEPHERD_CRITIC_EFFORT=high

# Plan-gate reviewer — adversarially critiques a plan before execution.
# @type=enum(inherit, claude, codex)
SHEPHERD_PLANNER_CLI=inherit
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_PLANNER_MODEL=default
# @type=enum(default, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra)
SHEPHERD_PLANNER_EFFORT=default

# Recap writer — summarises a session at the archive chokepoint.
# @type=enum(inherit, claude, codex)
SHEPHERD_RECAP_CLI=claude
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_RECAP_MODEL=sonnet
# @type=enum(default, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra)
SHEPHERD_RECAP_EFFORT=low

# Namer — turns a task prompt into a short session name.
# @type=enum(inherit, claude, codex)
SHEPHERD_NAMER_CLI=claude
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_NAMER_MODEL=haiku
# @type=enum(default, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra)
SHEPHERD_NAMER_EFFORT=low

# LLM-backed session naming. Kill switch — default ON; `0` keeps the pure-heuristic name.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_LLM_NAMING=true

# Autopilot — decides the next move for an unattended session.
# @type=enum(inherit, claude, codex)
SHEPHERD_AUTOPILOT_CLI=claude
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_AUTOPILOT_MODEL=haiku
# @type=enum(default, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra)
SHEPHERD_AUTOPILOT_EFFORT=low
# Maximum autopilot steps per session before it stops nudging.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_AUTOPILOT_STEP_CAP=10

# Distiller — turns captured session learnings into proposed house rules.
# @type=enum(inherit, claude, codex)
SHEPHERD_DISTILLER_CLI=inherit
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_DISTILLER_MODEL=default
# @type=enum(default, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra)
SHEPHERD_DISTILLER_EFFORT=default
# Days between distiller runs.
# @type=number
SHEPHERD_DISTILLER_INTERVAL_DAYS=1

# Optimizer — one-click repo-instruction improvement.
# @type=enum(inherit, claude, codex)
SHEPHERD_OPTIMIZER_CLI=inherit
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_OPTIMIZER_MODEL=default
# @type=enum(default, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra)
SHEPHERD_OPTIMIZER_EFFORT=default

# Merge-suggest — proposes a merge order for the open PR queue.
# @type=enum(inherit, claude, codex)
SHEPHERD_MERGE_SUGGEST_CLI=inherit
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_MERGE_SUGGEST_MODEL=default
# @type=enum(default, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra)
SHEPHERD_MERGE_SUGGEST_EFFORT=default

# Judge (#2369) — opt-in; routes the autopilot stop classifier through a metered "System One"
# decision API instead of a transient `claude` spawn. Arming needs BOTH this flag and JEV_API_KEY
# below: that key is also the eval harness's credential, so its presence alone must not arm a
# billed production path, and the judge must be disarmable without removing it. On any failure —
# transport, deadline, spend ceiling — the classifier falls back to the spawn, so turning this on
# cannot cost a capability. Seeds a fresh DB; persisted + UI-configurable.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_JUDGE=false
# TypeSafe AI (JEV) key, read by BOTH the server (when SHEPHERD_JUDGE is on) and the eval harness's
# `--backend jev` leg. Operator-supplied (`~/.shepherd/env` for the server, `~/.shepherd/eval.env`
# for the eval), never CI-injected. Absent by default: the judge stays unarmed whatever the flag
# says, and the eval leg reports CANNOT_RUN rather than failing.
# @sensitive
JEV_API_KEY=
# Decision model, PINNED to a snapshot. The vendor SDK's own default is a floating alias, under
# which a re-point would arrive as a silent accuracy change rather than a version bump.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_JUDGE_MODEL=jev-1.13.0
# API root. Configuration rather than a constant so the vendor-swap door stays open — this wire
# format has at least one self-hostable implementation.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_JUDGE_BASE_URL=https://api.typesafe.ai
# Daily USD ceiling for judge calls. Per-call cost is a small fraction of a cent, so this is a
# runaway guard, not a budget: on breach the classifier falls back to the spawn for the rest of the
# day and the operator gets one notification. Persisted + UI-configurable.
# @type=number(min=0)
SHEPHERD_JUDGE_DAILY_USD=1
# TOTAL wall-clock budget for one judge call, retries included. The vendor SDK's own timeout is
# per-attempt with no total budget, so without this a rate-limited call honouring `Retry-After` can
# outlast the 120s spawn the judge exists to be faster than.
# @type=number(isInt=true, min=1000, max=60000)
SHEPHERD_JUDGE_TIMEOUT_MS=8000
# How many days of judge spend rows the daily sweep keeps.
# @type=number(isInt=true, min=1, max=3650)
SHEPHERD_JUDGE_SPEND_RETENTION_DAYS=90

# Blocked-pane backstop (#2375) — the same decision model BEHIND the block regexes. A call is made
# only on a pane classifyBlocked already flagged as a menu/yes-no dialog, and the answer buys
# PATIENCE, never a decision: it can never promote a shape, pick an option or type into a PTY, only
# hold an unannounced card back for a few seconds so the pane can correct itself. "shadow" pays and
# logs but never delays (the measurement that has to justify arming); "armed" lets the probability
# hold. Every failure path announces immediately. Armed independently of SHEPHERD_JUDGE, but shares
# its key, model and daily ceiling. Seeds a fresh DB; persisted + UI-configurable.
# @type=enum(off, shadow, armed)
SHEPHERD_BLOCK_JUDGE=off
# How many days of backstop decision rows the daily sweep keeps. Shorter than the spend table's
# window because these rows carry terminal tails.
# @type=number(isInt=true, min=1, max=365)
SHEPHERD_BLOCK_JUDGE_LOG_RETENTION_DAYS=14

# House-rule relevance (#2376) — narrow the injected house-rules block to the rules this session's
# request is actually about. Needs the judge armed (SHEPHERD_JUDGE=1 + JEV_API_KEY); inert without
# it. `shadow` asks and records the verdicts WITHOUT acting on them, which is how you gather the
# evidence for `enforce` from real sessions. Seeds a fresh DB only; the Settings value then wins.
# @type=enum(off, shadow, enforce)
SHEPHERD_HOUSE_RULE_RELEVANCE=off
# Drop a candidate rule only when the judge's probability that the request is about it falls BELOW
# this. Asymmetric on purpose: everything the judge is unsure about keeps today's behaviour.
# Read via `envNum("KEY", default)`, so the auditor cannot see the reference; the bounds below are
# documentation, and the code clamps to the same [0,1] range.
# @type=number(min=0, max=1) @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_RELEVANCE_DROP_BELOW=0.35
# Most candidate rules one call may ask about. Overflow is injected unjudged, never dropped.
# Read via `envNum("KEY", default)`, so the auditor cannot see the reference.
# @type=number(isInt=true, min=1, max=255) @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_RELEVANCE_MAX=32
# How many days of relevance verdicts the daily sweep keeps. They deliberately outlive their
# session, so this sweep is the only thing that ever removes one.
# @type=number(isInt=true, min=1, max=3650)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_RELEVANCE_RETENTION_DAYS=90

# Doc agent — opt-in; keeps the docs site in sync with source changes.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_DOC_AGENT=false
# Whether a doc-agent run actually commits and opens a PR, rather than only drafting.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_DOC_AGENT_ACT=false
# @type=enum(inherit, claude, codex)
SHEPHERD_DOC_AGENT_CLI=inherit
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_DOC_AGENT_MODEL=default
# @type=enum(default, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra)
SHEPHERD_DOC_AGENT_EFFORT=low
# Local hour (0-23) for the nightly doc-agent sweep.
# @type=number(isInt=true, min=0, max=23)
SHEPHERD_DOC_AGENT_NIGHTLY_HOUR=3

# Maintain loop — opt-in nightly self-maintenance: evaluation, logging and diagnosis spawn.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_MAINTAIN_LOOP=false
# A drafted issue is actually filed. Meaningless without SHEPHERD_MAINTAIN_LOOP.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_MAINTAIN_ACT=false
# A Tier-3 fix actually opens a PR. Deliberately independent of SHEPHERD_MAINTAIN_ACT.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_MAINTAIN_PR=false
# Local hour (0-23) for the maintain loop.
# @type=number(isInt=true, min=0, max=23)
SHEPHERD_MAINTAIN_HOUR=4
# @type=enum(inherit, claude, codex)
SHEPHERD_MAINTAIN_CLI=inherit
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_MAINTAIN_MODEL=default
# @type=enum(default, low, medium, high, xhigh, max, ultra)
SHEPHERD_MAINTAIN_EFFORT=default
# JSON object overriding the maintain loop's band thresholds; merged over the built-in defaults.
# Unparseable input silently falls back to the defaults.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_MAINTAIN_THRESHOLDS=

# ── Review, merge train and spend ────────────────────────────────────────────

# How many critic→fix cycles a PR gets before the session stops re-reviewing.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_REVIEW_CYCLES_CAP=3

# Same, for plan-gate review rounds.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_PLAN_REVIEW_CYCLES_CAP=5

# Hard deadline for a single critic run before it is abandoned with an `error` verdict.
# Clamped to 60000-3600000; an unparseable value falls back to the default.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_REVIEW_TIMEOUT_MS=600000

# How many times the merge train will rebase a PR onto a moved base before giving up.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_AUTOMERGE_REBASE_CAP=5

# Extra-credit ceiling, in currency units, that autonomous drain may spend. `0` disables.
# @type=number
SHEPHERD_EXTRA_CREDITS_DRAIN_CEILING=0

# Minimum gap between two pushes from the same session, in milliseconds.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_PUSH_COOLDOWN_MS=120000

# Send fewer, coarser web-push notifications.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_REDUCED_PUSH_MODE=false

# ── Learnings lifecycle ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# The admission and retirement machinery for distilled house rules. Counts are per sweep;
# "N" is the number of observations backing a rule.

# Promote qualifying proposed learnings to active trials. Kill switch — default ON.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_AUTO_TRIAL=true

# Minimum observations before a proposed learning may enter trial.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_TRIAL_NMIN=4

# Minimum distinct sessions contributing those observations.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_TRIAL_SESSION_FLOOR=2

# Minimum distinct evidence kinds a candidate must span.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_TRIAL_MIN_KINDS=2

# Minimum distinct sessions a candidate must span.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_TRIAL_MIN_SESSIONS=3

# Cap on promotions per sweep.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_MAX_TRIAL_PER_SWEEP=3

# A trial with fewer than this many observations is eligible for reaping once stale.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_TRIAL_REAP_NMIN=8

# Days of inactivity after which an under-evidenced trial is reaped.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_TRIAL_REAP_DAYS=21

# Hard age ceiling: a trial older than this is reaped regardless of evidence.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_TRIAL_REAP_MAX_DAYS=60

# Cap on trial reaps per sweep.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_MAX_REAP_PER_SWEEP=5

# Permanently prune proposed learnings whose latest evidence is older than this many days.
# Applied in full each sweep — no cap, no exemption.
# @type=number
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_PRUNE_DAYS=3

# z-score for the Wilson lower bound used to score a rule's help rate.
# @type=number
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_WILSON_Z=1.96

# Minimum observations before an active rule may be auto-retired.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_RETIRE_NMIN=8

# Prior help-rate assumed for a rule with no evidence yet.
# @type=number
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_BASE_RATE=0.5

# Observations needed before the measured base rate replaces the assumed one.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_BASE_RATE_MIN_N=20

# Cap on auto-retirements per sweep.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_MAX_RETIRE_PER_SWEEP=3

# ── Usage hold and downgrade ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Queue newly submitted tasks instead of spawning them while account usage is high.
# Kill switch — default ON; `0`/`false` always spawns immediately.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_USAGE_HOLD_ENABLED=true

# Hold threshold: when the higher of the 5-hour / weekly usage window reaches this percent,
# new tasks are held. Clamped to 0-100.
# @type=number(isInt=true, min=0, max=100)
SHEPHERD_USAGE_HOLD_PCT=80

# Auto-start held tasks once usage drops back below the threshold. Kill switch — default ON;
# `0`/`false` keeps them queued until the operator acts.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_USAGE_HOLD_AUTO_RELEASE=true

# Companion to the hold: run every newly spawned agent on the downgrade model once usage
# reaches the downgrade threshold, so work keeps flowing more cheaply. Opt-in.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_USAGE_DOWNGRADE_ENABLED=false

# Usage percent at which the downgrade kicks in. Clamped to 0-100.
# @type=number(isInt=true, min=0, max=100)
SHEPHERD_USAGE_DOWNGRADE_PCT=70

# Model every agent falls back to while downgraded.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_USAGE_DOWNGRADE_MODEL=haiku

# ── Preview servers ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Expose preview ports over `tailscale serve` automatically. Kill switch — default ON;
# `0` leaves the range to be managed manually.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_PREVIEW_AUTO_SERVE=true

# First port of the preview range. Validated at boot against the main, ingress and served ports.
# @type=port
SHEPHERD_PREVIEW_PORT_BASE=8001

# How many consecutive ports the preview range covers.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_PREVIEW_PORT_COUNT=16

# Interval of the sweep that detects `.shepherd-preview` port hints, in milliseconds.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_PREVIEW_SWEEP_MS=4000

# Grace period before a preview process that ignored SIGTERM is SIGKILLed, in milliseconds.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_PREVIEW_KILL_MAX_AGE_MS=10000

# Stop an idle preview server after this many milliseconds. `0` disables idle stopping.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_PREVIEW_IDLE_STOP_MS=0

# ── Temp-dir and inode guard ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Root the tmp sweep walks. Default: CLAUDE_CODE_TMPDIR, else `<tmpdir>/claude-$uid`.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_TMP_SWEEP_DIR=

# Disk-backed NODE_COMPILE_CACHE dir, deliberately off tmpfs so the cache stops eating tmpfs
# inodes. Default `~/.cache/shepherd/node-compile-cache`.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_NODE_COMPILE_CACHE=

# TMPDIR handed to spawned agents. Default `~/.cache/shepherd/tmp`; the empty string disables
# the redirect entirely and leaves agents on tmpfs.
# @type=string
SHEPHERD_AGENT_TMPDIR=

# Inode-usage percent above which the tmp sweep runs. Also the diagnostics warning band.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_TMP_INODE_PCT=80

# Entry-count above which the tmp sweep runs. Also the diagnostics warning band.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_TMP_ENTRY_LIMIT=1000

# Age in hours past which a scratch entry counts as stale and is swept.
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_TMP_STALE_HOURS=24

# ── Developer and operator toggles ───────────────────────────────────────────

# Sample event-loop lag and emit a profile. Diagnostic only.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_PROFILE_LOOP=false

# Connect Remote Control at startup rather than on demand.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_REMOTE_CONTROL_AT_STARTUP=false

# Run the terminal UI fullscreen.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_TUI_FULLSCREEN=false

# Disable mouse reporting in the terminal UI.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_TUI_DISABLE_MOUSE=false

# Skip the CLI picker in the Up-Next flow and use the configured default.
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_UPNEXT_SKIP_CLI_PICKER=false

# ── Local tooling: pre-push and verification scripts ─────────────────────────

# Override the pre-push lane concurrency cap, which is otherwise sized from core count.
# Contributor-only: steers scripts/pre-push.ts on a developer's machine, never a running
# Shepherd, so it is deliberately absent from the operator Configuration page.
# @docsExempt
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_PREPUSH_LANES=

# Override every pre-push lane's wall-clock timeout, in milliseconds. Also caps the trailing
# fallow step, which otherwise gets 300000. Contributor-only, like SHEPHERD_PREPUSH_LANES.
# @docsExempt
# @type=number(isInt=true)
SHEPHERD_PREPUSH_LANE_TIMEOUT_MS=

# Run the opt-in app-binding scroll matrix in scripts/verify-herdr-terminal.ts (same as --scroll).
# Contributor-only: a flag for that verification script, read by nothing the server runs.
# @docsExempt
# @type=boolean
SHEPHERD_VERIFY_SCROLL=false

# ── Ambient process environment ──────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Not Shepherd's to set — supplied by systemd, git, the test runner or the operator's shell.
# Declared because the scanner sees them and would otherwise fail the gate.

# systemd's per-start invocation id, used to tell a restart of THIS unit from a fresh boot.
# @type=string
INVOCATION_ID=

# `test` makes the membrane-launch probe throw instead of reaching its host-spawning default.
# @type=string
NODE_ENV=

# git identity for commits Shepherd makes on the operator's behalf. Defaults below are what
# the server falls back to when the ambient environment does not set them.
# @type=string
GIT_AUTHOR_NAME=Shepherd
# @type=string
GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL=shepherd@local
# @type=string
GIT_COMMITTER_NAME=Shepherd
# @type=string
GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL=shepherd@local

# ── CI-injected: GitHub Actions workflow inputs ──────────────────────────────
#
# Set by workflow YAML for the helper scripts under scripts/, never by an operator or the
# server. Listed so the gate stays green and so the workflow contract is discoverable.

# Anthropic API key for the live eval harness and the issue-triage bot. Absent locally, which
# is why both degrade instead of failing.
# @sensitive
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# Model the issue-triage bot calls. Default `claude-haiku-4-5`.
# @type=string
ANTHROPIC_MODEL=

# Base ref the announcement-version check diffs against. Default `origin/main`.
# @type=string
BASE_REF=

# Docs root the issue-triage bot searches. Default `docs-site/src/content/docs`.
# @type=string
DOCS_DIR=

# Path to the Actions step-output file the issue-triage bot writes to.
# @type=string
GITHUB_OUTPUT=

# The triaged issue's title and body, passed in rather than re-fetched.
# @type=string
ISSUE_TITLE=
# @type=string
ISSUE_BODY=

# Whether the issue bot answers questions. Opt-in: only the literal string `true` enables it.
# @type=boolean
ISSUE_BOT_ANSWER_QUESTIONS=false

# Whether the issue bot comments on bug/feature issues. Kill switch — only the literal string
# `false` disables it.
# @type=boolean
ISSUE_BOT_COMMENT_ON_BUG_FEATURE=true

# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# CATALOGUED BUT NOT GATED
#
# Everything below carries `@auditIgnore`, because `varlock audit` cannot see its read
# site — a shell script, a destructured `env.KEY`, a `process.env[SOME_CONST]` lookup, or a
# key passed to a helper as a string. They are declared so this file stays a complete
# catalogue, but the gate will never tell you when one is added, removed or renamed.
#
# NOT declared, deliberately: identifiers that match a `SHEPHERD_*` grep but are TypeScript
# constants, not environment variables — SHEPHERD_IGNORE_GLOB, SHEPHERD_EXCLUDE_START,
# SHEPHERD_EXCLUDE_END (src/shepherd-exclude.ts), SHEPHERD_KEY_OK_8F3A (src/verify-key.ts),
# SHEPHERD_ISSUE_LOG_MARKER (src/forge/types.ts), SHEPHERD_UPDATE_EXIT__ and
# SHEPHERD_DISCARD_STALE (src/update.ts markers), SHEPHERD_CAPTURE_EXTENSION_ID and
# SHEPHERD_CAPTURE_UNPACKED_DEV_ID (src/config.ts), SHEPHERD_HERDR_COMMANDS
# (scripts/herdr-compat/cli-surface.ts), SHEPHERD_VERSION (src/version.ts — the package
# version, re-exported for the /health payload).
#
# Also NOT declared: the ambient POSIX/session variables Shepherd consumes but does not own —
# HOME, PATH, TERM, LANG, USER and XDG_RUNTIME_DIR. varlock's scanner ignores these by design
# (verified: it reports none of them missing), they are supplied by the OS and login session
# rather than configured, and documenting Shepherd's defaults for them would be meaningless.
# ═════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

# ── Host state paths (read via destructured `env.KEY`) ───────────────────────

# Host-global Shepherd state dir, the stable `$HOME` anchor the host lock uses.
# Default `~/.shepherd`.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_STATE_DIR=

# Destination dir for the hourly SQLite backups. Default: `backups/` next to the DB.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_BACKUP_DIR=

# Escape hatch for the in-pane session/socket conflict: when Shepherd runs inside a herdr pane
# and a non-`default` HERDR_SESSION disagrees with the inherited HERDR_SOCKET_PATH, `1`
# suppresses the override and keeps the inherited socket.
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_HERDR_IGNORE_SESSION=false

# ── Learnings ranking weights (read via `envNum("KEY", default)`) ────────────

# Weight of recency in a rule's rank score.
# @type=number @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_RANK_W_RECENCY=0.5

# Weight of measured helpfulness in a rule's rank score.
# @type=number @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_RANK_W_HELP=0.5

# Half-life in days for the recency decay.
# @type=number @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_RANK_HALF_LIFE_DAYS=30

# Strength of the prior, in pseudo-observations.
# @type=number @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_RANK_PRIOR_STRENGTH=4

# The neutral prior a rule starts from before any evidence.
# @type=number @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_LEARNINGS_RANK_NEUTRAL_PRIOR=0.5

# ── herdr pane environment ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# herdr exports these into every pane it opens, so Shepherd reads them to tell "I am running
# inside a herdr pane" from "I am the server". Read via a destructured `env.KEY`
# (src/herdr-session.ts, src/herdr-recovery.ts), which the scanner cannot see — unlike
# HERDR_SOCKET_PATH, which is also read as a plain process.env and so is gated above.

# herdr session name. Resolves the per-session socket path when HERDR_SOCKET_PATH is unset.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
HERDR_SESSION=default

# Set to 1 by herdr inside a pane. When it is 1 and a non-`default` HERDR_SESSION disagrees
# with the pane-inherited HERDR_SOCKET_PATH, Shepherd prefers its own per-session socket and
# warns, so a dev instance cannot silently attach to the parent pane's herd (#1596).
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
HERDR_ENV=false

# ── Injected into spawned agents and preview scripts ─────────────────────────

# The owning session's id, stamped into every agent spawn. The reaper attributes an orphaned
# process by finding this in its /proc/<pid>/environ, and the agent control plane uses it to
# address its own session.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_SESSION_ID=

# Base URL of the agent-ingress API, handed to agents so they can call back (e.g. rename).
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_AGENT_API_URL=

# The session worktree path, exported into the generated preview script.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_WORKTREE_PATH=

# Set to 1 inside a generated preview script, so a dev server can tell it was launched by
# Shepherd's preview machinery.
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_PREVIEW=false

# Log file the generated preview script appends to.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_PREVIEW_LOG=

# Preferred first port for a preview script's own search. Falls back to
# SHEPHERD_PREVIEW_PORT_BASE, then 5174.
# @type=port @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_PREVIEW_PORT=

# ── Third-party variables pinned onto spawned children (NOT exhaustive) ──────
#
# Not Shepherd's own namespace: knobs belonging to Claude Code, git and node that Shepherd sets
# on the processes it spawns. Declared because they explain behaviour an operator can see in a
# pane — not because this list is complete. See the header.

# Set to 1 on an agent's env when the TUI runs fullscreen or with mouse reporting off, so
# Claude Code stops grabbing the mouse.
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_MOUSE=false

# Set to 1 instead when the TUI runs fullscreen — Claude Code's flicker-free renderer.
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
CLAUDE_CODE_NO_FLICKER=false

# Set to 1 when the TUI is NOT fullscreen, and on every wrapped spawn unless the caller already
# chose a renderer: keeps Claude Code out of the alternate screen buffer so the pane keeps its
# scrollback.
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
CLAUDE_CODE_DISABLE_ALTERNATE_SCREEN=false

# Pinned to "false" on spawned agents to disable the claude.ai account-connector MCP servers.
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
ENABLE_CLAUDEAI_MCP_SERVERS=true

# Pinned to 1 on a pinned `claude` spawn so the CLI does not update itself mid-session.
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
DISABLE_AUTOUPDATER=false

# Set on every wrapped spawn to the agent scratch dir (see SHEPHERD_AGENT_TMPDIR) so agents
# write scratch to disk instead of tmpfs. Only set when the caller did not supply one.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
TMPDIR=

# Set on every wrapped spawn to the disk-backed compile cache (see SHEPHERD_NODE_COMPILE_CACHE),
# deliberately off tmpfs so the cache stops eating tmpfs inodes.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
NODE_COMPILE_CACHE=

# Pinned to 0 on git invocations so git can never block on an interactive credential prompt
# inside a non-interactive server process.
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
GIT_TERMINAL_PROMPT=false

# Pinned to 1 when managing plugins, so a machine-level git config cannot influence the result.
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=false

# Pins the prettier copy the doc agent formats with, so it cannot auto-install an unpinned
# version whose formatting differs from the repo's.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_PRETTIER_MODULE=

# ── herdr recovery worker handshake ──────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Set by the parent on the detached recovery worker it spawns; read back by that worker.

# Marks the child process as the recovery worker.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_HERDR_RECOVERY_WORKER=

# Whether the worker should restart the herdr server after recovering.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_HERDR_RECOVERY_RESTART=

# herdr binary the worker should drive.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_HERDR_RECOVERY_BIN=

# The runtime status the worker expects to find, so it can bail if the situation changed.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_HERDR_RECOVERY_EXPECTED=

# Where the worker writes its log. NOTE: unlike its siblings above this one IS read as a
# plain `process.env.SHEPHERD_HERDR_RECOVERY_LOG` (src/herdr-recovery.ts), so it looks like it
# belongs in the gated section — but the scanner cannot see that read either, because a regex
# literal earlier in the same file blinds it (see the header). Dropping @auditIgnore here
# turns the gate RED with a false "Unused in schema"; verified, do not "fix" it.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_HERDR_RECOVERY_LOG=

# Per-probe timeout in milliseconds. Accepted range 10-30000; anything else falls back.
# @type=number(isInt=true) @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_HERDR_RECOVERY_TIMEOUT_MS=10000

# Poll interval in milliseconds. Accepted range 10-30000.
# @type=number(isInt=true) @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_HERDR_RECOVERY_POLL_MS=250

# Whole-recovery deadline in milliseconds. Accepted range 10-30000.
# @type=number(isInt=true) @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_HERDR_RECOVERY_GLOBAL_TIMEOUT_MS=30000

# ── Deploy shell scripts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# Read by deploy/*.sh, which the scanner cannot parse at all.

# Install dir. Default `~/.shepherd/app`, matching the systemd unit's WorkingDirectory.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_DIR=

# Git ref the installer clones or checks out.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_REF=main

# Local source override for the installer: a tarball file (extracted into $SHEPHERD_DIR) or a
# directory (copied into it), instead of cloning.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_SRC=

# Source deploy/install.sh as a library (define its functions, run nothing). Test seam.
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_INSTALL_LIB=false

# Skip installing the systemd unit; provision.ts then prints the manual-start hint.
# @type=boolean @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_NO_SERVICE=false

# Test seams overriding `uname -s` / `uname -m` during platform detection.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_UNAME_S=
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_UNAME_M=

# Log file rotated hourly by shepherd-logrotate.timer. Default `~/.shepherd/shepherd.log`.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_LOG=

# Rotate once the log exceeds this many bytes (50 MiB).
# @type=number(isInt=true) @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_LOG_MAX_BYTES=52428800

# How many rotated logs to keep.
# @type=number(isInt=true) @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_LOG_KEEP=7

# ── Update handshake (server → transient update unit) ────────────────────────
#
# Passed as `--setenv=` on the transient unit and read by deploy/update.sh. All four must be
# present together or the discard path refuses to run.

# Signature of the working tree at confirmation time; update.sh aborts if it no longer matches.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_DISCARD_SIG=

# Scratch dir holding the pathspec files; removed by update.sh on exit.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_DISCARD_DIR=

# NUL-delimited pathspec file listing everything to discard.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_DISCARD_PATHSPEC_ALL=

# NUL-delimited pathspec file listing the working-tree-only subset.
# @type=string @auditIgnore
SHEPHERD_DISCARD_PATHSPEC_WT=
